post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

omarchy-crt is installed. Two steps are left, and both are yours to take:

  1. hand the DAC's connector to omarchy-crt at every boot:
       sudo systemctl enable --now omarchy-crt-lease.service
     The connector defaults to HDMI-A-1. For another one:
       sudo systemctl edit omarchy-crt-lease.service
     and set Environment=OMARCHY_CRT_CONNECTOR=HDMI-A-2

  2. install the bar plugin into your own session (not as root):
       /usr/share/omarchy-crt/omarchy-crt-install --no-build

Then check the setup with:  omarchy-crt doctor

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'

omarchy-crt upgraded. If the bar plugin looks stale, refresh it with:
  /usr/share/omarchy-crt/omarchy-crt-install --no-build

MSG
}

pre_remove() {
  systemctl disable --now omarchy-crt-lease.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
